(1527, 'C2112094002540034', 10, 254, '54', NULL, 'Attn: Sabekun Nahar Shirin, Deputy Director, FICSD, Bangladesh Bank.\r\n\r\nDear Madam,                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \r\n\r\nGreetings from MTB Service Quality Department!\r\n\r\nWith reference to your below email, dated, December 6, 2021, we would like to inform you that MTB has already replied to the said demand notice through an enlisted legal counsel. It has been found that due to non-adjustment of the outstanding liabilities of Tk. 420,839,490.91 (Taka Forty Two Crore Eight Lac Thirty Nine Thousand Four Hundred Ninety and Ninety One Paisa) since 2012, MTB did not agree to issue NOC based on the said resignations by the directors of the company. The decision has been informed to the concerned party several times. \r\n\r\nThe reply to the demand notice by MTB enlisted legal counsel is attached herewith the email. Hope this will suffice.\r\n\r\nWe would like to take the opportunity to thank you for the usual support and co-operation from Bangladesh bank and wish to continue to receive the same in the days to come! From now on you can also send us email at our department group email sq@mutualtrustbank.com for our convenience.\r\n\r\nKind regards.\r\n\r\nShadman Sakib\r\nAssociate\r\nService Quality Department\r\nMutual Trust Bank Limited \r\nCorporate Head Office, MTB Centre\r\nWeb: www.mutualtrustbank.com', 'Replied to BB.', NULL, 'Ban', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Loans and Advances', NULL, NULL, '2021-12-09 15:32:39', '2021-12-09 15:32:39', NULL, '6', NULL),
