(3572, 'C2110051000230041', 18, 490, '19', NULL, 'The acquirer has re-presented our dispute with attached document. So the transactions will not be reversed and informed customer about the feedback. Acquirer Message: ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã…â€œAs per Dalalplus Terms and Condition, under section 22 (Refund) it was clearly stated that \"In case of any cancellations of any order(s) by customers the paid amount would be refunded as the customers dalalplus account firstly. Customer need to report an issue as refund category and should mention his/her desired refund type(i.e. bkash/bank) alongside details (bkash personal number, bank account details). If any order got canceled by customers, then the customer will get refunded with his/her principal amount (paid amount). The refund process may take up to 30 working days or more depending upon the payment service gateway provider s clauses. The customer won t be eligible for any extra cashback/bonus against his principal amount in case of refunds. Dalalplus isn t bound to pay any kind of service fee or cost for the refunded amount.\". Additionally, under section 7 (Losses) it was clearly stated that \"We won t be in charge of any business or individual misfortunes (counting however not restricted to loss of advantages , income, contracts, foreseen investment , information, altruism, or squandered consumption) or whatever other backhanded or weighty misfortune that may not sensibly predictable to both you and us once you initiated utilizing the location .\" From above scenario, it is clear that at the time of purchase, cardholder read and agreed merchants Terms and condition and return policy box that was disclosed properly with him/her. So, cardholder claim is invalid as merchant policy was properly disclosed while transaction. Please find attached merchant T&C as reference which is also available at merchant website.ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã‚Â', 'The acquirer has re-presented our dispute with attached document. So the transactions will not be reversed and informed customer about the feedback. Acquirer Message: ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã…â€œAs per Dalalplus Terms and Condition, under section 22 (Refund) it was clearly stated that \"In case of any cancellations of any order(s) by customers the paid amount would be refunded as the customers dalalplus account firstly. Customer need to report an issue as refund category and should mention his/her desired refund type(i.e. bkash/bank) alongside details (bkash personal number, bank account details). If any order got canceled by customers, then the customer will get refunded with his/her principal amount (paid amount). The refund process may take up to 30 working days or more depending upon the payment service gateway provider s clauses. The customer won t be eligible for any extra cashback/bonus against his principal amount in case of refunds. Dalalplus isn t bound to pay any kind of service fee or cost for the refunded amount.\". Additionally, under section 7 (Losses) it was clearly stated that \"We won t be in charge of any business or individual misfortunes (counting however not restricted to loss of advantages , income, contracts, foreseen investment , information, altruism, or squandered consumption) or whatever other backhanded or weighty misfortune that may not sensibly predictable to both you and us once you initiated utilizing the location .\" From above scenario, it is clear that at the time of purchase, cardholder read and agreed merchants Terms and condition and return policy box that was disclosed properly with him/her. So, cardholder claim is invalid as merchant policy was properly disclosed while transaction. Please find attached merchant T&C as reference which is also available at merchant website.ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã‚Â', 0, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Yes', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2022-01-31 17:34:11', '2022-01-31 17:34:11', NULL, '104', NULL),
