(11767, 'C2209051001990043', 9, 199, '20', NULL, '1.	MTB imposed VAT on the first 10 transactions that were settled under Merchant Category Code 4816 (computer network & information services) according to the BRPD Circular Letter no. 4, dated, 03 March 2019. On the other hand, the other, 2 transactions were settled under MCC 7392 (Management, Consulting, and Public Relations Services) that were exempted from VAT. \r\n\r\n2.	Whenever a customer pays credit card bill in USD, he/she effectively buys dollars from the bank at the prevailing exchange rate. Hence, a customer needs to pay the foreign currency bill at the exchange rate of the payment date. \r\n\r\n3.	MTB always mentions the settlement date in the statement. Hence, there should not be any room for confusion.\r\n\r\n4.	VAT is imposed on all fees & charges as per Schedule of Charges (SOC).', 'Reply has been sent to BB.', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2022-09-11 11:58:45', '2022-09-11 11:58:45', NULL, '104', 'No'),
