(12440, 'C2209272004980041', 18, 498, '297', NULL, 'USD 12,173.00  and USD 5,747.00 were disbursed on June 30, 2022 after deducting 2% source tax according to the Section 52AA of Income Tax Ordinance 1984. Besides, USD 2,337.00 was disbursed on November 11, 2022 on which 3% source tax was deducted according to Section 52 of Income Tax Ordinance 1984. \r\n\r\nLater on, our concerned department communicated with NBR after having objection from the customer regarding the source tax. After verifying all the documents which were provided by the customer, NBR advised us to follow the Income Finance Act 2021 and Income Tax Paripatra 2021-2022. It was found from Income Tax Paripatra 2021-2022 (section 52Q) that 10% tax was supposed to be deducted for service and 7.50% for supply of goods instead of 3%. In this regards, we have communicated the same to the customer and requested him to keep the rest of the amount available in his account. After acknowledging the information, the customer declared that he will deposit the remaining amount after having a discussion with NBR in this regard. Hope this suffices your query.', 'USD 12,173.00  and USD 5,747.00 were disbursed on June 30, 2022 after deducting 2% source tax according to the Section 52AA of Income Tax Ordinance 1984. Besides, USD 2,337.00 was disbursed on November 11, 2022 on which 3% source tax was deducted according to Section 52 of Income Tax Ordinance 1984.   Later on, our concerned department communicated with NBR after having objection from the customer regarding the source tax. After verifying all the documents which were provided by the customer, NBR advised us to follow the Income Finance Act 2021 and Income Tax Paripatra 2021-2022. It was found from Income Tax Paripatra 2021-2022 (section 52Q) that 10% tax was supposed to be deducted for service and 7.50% for supply of goods instead of 3%. In this regards, we have communicated the same to the customer and requested him to keep the rest of the amount available in his account. After acknowledging the information, the customer declared that he will deposit the remaining amount after having a discussion with NBR in this regard. Hope this suffices your query.', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- Yes', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Remittance', NULL, NULL, '2022-09-29 10:50:25', '2022-09-29 10:50:25', NULL, '6', 'No'),
