(14395, 'C2211061002190035', 9, 219, '20', NULL, '1.	MTB imposed VAT on transactions associated with boosting on Facebook as per BRPD Circular Letter no. 4, dated, March 03, 2019. However, the mentioned 15% VAT was deducted from Facebook at the time of transaction.\r\n2.	VAT is imposed after settlement of any transaction. Customers only receive SMS of successful transaction. However, the said VAT amount is reflected in cardholderÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s next statement and it is also available in smart banking app.  \r\n3.	In response to the issue no. 3 & 4 of the customerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s letter, this is to inform you that some authorized transactions may get settled immediately, while others may take days or even weeks to get settled. This completely depends on the merchant. When the merchant initiates the settlement, the network (Visa/Master Card etc.) charges the bank based on the prevailing rate on the settlement date. Accordingly bank charges the customers.\r\n4.	As per the global practice of all card issuers, transactional notification is sent immediately once any transaction is authorized/approved. Moreover, the settlement amount and date are available in card statement for customers.', '1.	MTB imposed VAT on transactions associated with boosting on Facebook as per BRPD Circular Letter no. 4, dated, March 03, 2019. However, the mentioned 15% VAT was deducted from Facebook at the time of transaction. 2.	VAT is imposed after settlement of any transaction. Customers only receive SMS of successful transaction. However, the said VAT amount is reflected in cardholderÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s next statement and it is also available in smart banking app.   3.	In response to the issue no. 3 & 4 of the customerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s letter, this is to inform you that some authorized transactions may get settled immediately, while others may take days or even weeks to get settled. This completely depends on the merchant. When the merchant initiates the settlement, the network (Visa/Master Card etc.) charges the bank based on the prevailing rate on the settlement date. Accordingly bank charges the customers. 4.	As per the global practice of all card issuers, transactional notification is sent immediately once any transaction is authorized/approved. Moreover, the settlement amount and date are available in card statement for customers.', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2022-11-15 15:59:58', '2022-11-15 15:59:58', NULL, '104', 'No'),
