(18890, 'C2302081002190024', 9, 204, '20', NULL, 'Customer claimed that unauthorized charges are deducted from his account. Investigation reveals that no unauthorized charges have been deducted from the customerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s account. Credit Card fees and charges are imposed in accordance with the declared schedule of charges of the bank. The fees and charges are clearly mentioned on the bankÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s website as well as in the credit card application form, which was duly signed by the cardholder.', 'No unauthorized charges have been deducted from the customerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s account. Credit Card fees and charges are imposed in accordance with the declared schedule of charges of the bank. All the fees and charges are clearly mentioned on the bankÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s website as well as in the credit card application form, which was duly signed by the cardholder. Accordingly, We have replied to BB through letter ref: MTB/CHO/SQ/2023/04 .', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2023-02-22 11:06:10', '2023-02-22 11:06:10', NULL, '104', 'No'),
(18891, 'C2302156000630020', 4, 63, '42', NULL, 'The MFS transfer failed due to technical glitch.', 'The problem is fixed. CC tried to reach the customer but failed.', 0, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Yes', NULL, NULL, 'Internet Banking', NULL, NULL, '2023-02-22 11:11:15', '2023-02-22 11:11:15', NULL, '6', 'Yes'),
(18892, 'C2302086002070018', 9, 207, '275', NULL, 'Our investigation reveals that the SMS alert fee of BDT 230/- was deducted from customerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s account on 30-12-2022. However, as per customer request, we have deactivated the SMS alert service and the amount that was deducted has also been refunded to customerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s account on 05-01-2023.', 'The SMS alert fee of BDT 230/- was deducted from customerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s account on 30-12-2022. However, as per customer request, we have deactivated the SMS alert service and the amount that was deducted has also been refunded to customerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s account on 05-01-2023. Accordingly, We have replied to BB through letter ref: MTB/CHO/SQ/2023/08 dated 16 Feb 2023 .', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'General Banking', NULL, NULL, '2023-02-22 11:13:17', '2023-02-22 11:13:17', NULL, '49', 'No'),
(18893, 'C2302153007100029', 10, 710, '244', NULL, 'According to service request (S2302163003070071), branch forwarded the request on 16/02/23. Whereas, the customer placed the request to branch on 9/02/23. As a result, the process delayed.', 'Mobile number has been changed.', 0, 'Yes', NULL, NULL, 'Yes', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2023-02-22 11:17:53', '2023-02-22 11:17:53', NULL, '92', 'No'),
(18894, 'C2302081004790023', 12, 479, '19', NULL, 'Our investigation reveals that we have received the payment instruction from NRB Commercial Bank through Bangladesh BankÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s BEFTN Settlement report (attached) on 09-01-2023 (2nd session), for which the settlement date fell on 10-01-2023 (as per BB rules). We have successfully posted the BEFTN transaction on the settlement date and subsequently the payment was updated against the credit card on the same day (10-01-2023). There was no delay at our end for the aforementioned transaction.', 'Our investigation reveals that we have received the payment instruction from NRB Commercial Bank through Bangladesh BankÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s BEFTN Settlement report (attached) on 09-01-2023 (2nd session), for which the settlement date fell on 10-01-2023 (as per BB rules). We have successfully posted the BEFTN transaction on the settlement date and subsequently the payment was updated against the credit card on the same day (10-01-2023). There was no delay at our end for the aforementioned transaction. The customer may inquire with NRB Commercial Bank for sending the instruction to MTB on 09-01-2023 despite his account got debited on 30-12-2022. Accordingly, We have replied to BB through letter ref: MTB/CHO/SQ/2023/05 dated 16 Feb 2023.', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2023-02-22 11:24:49', '2023-02-22 11:24:49', NULL, '104', 'No'),
(18895, 'C2302136000480029', 4, 48, '10', NULL, 'Contact Center has already informed this issue to customer regarding the resolution', 'Contact Center has already informed this issue to customer regarding the resolution', 0, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Yes', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2023-02-22 11:27:27', '2023-02-22 11:27:27', NULL, '6', 'No'),
(18896, 'C2302081002040021', 9, 204, '20', NULL, 'Investigation reveals that MPP (MTB protection plan) fee was imposed against the mentioned credit card. MTB Protection Plan is an insurance coverage program offered to all credit cardholders. Initially, MTB Protection Plan facility was complementary for Signature credit cardholderÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s but now the bank has decided to impose an MPP fee on Signature cardholders from October 2022 after notifying the customer through SMS. However, if any cardholder is not willing to avail the insurance coverage then he/she may de-enroll the plan.', 'MPP (MTB protection plan) fee was imposed against the mentioned credit card. Please note that MTB Protection Plan is an insurance coverage program offered to all credit cardholders. Initially, MTB Protection Plan facility was complementary for Signature credit cardholderÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s but now the bank has decided to impose an MPP fee on Signature cardholders from October 2022 after notifying the customer through SMS. However, if any cardholder is not willing to avail the insurance coverage then he/she may de-enroll the plan. We have already reversed the MPP fee (December 2022) for the cardholder and de-enrolled the MTB Protection Plan as per his request. Accordingly, we have replied to BB through letter ref: MTB/CHO/SQ/2023/07 dated 16 Feb 2023 .', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2023-02-22 11:38:52', '2023-02-22 11:38:52', NULL, '104', 'No'),
(18897, 'C2302011006650045', 13, 665, '18', NULL, 'There is a system limitation in mrewardz portal. For domestic air ticket purchase, the customer require passport number which is unnecessary.', 'Card business team discussed the issue with GIIFT team to remove passport number field and place NID field instead to purchase domestic air ticket. Besides the technical issue which the customer mentioned is resolved now. Business team requested the customer to try now.', 0, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Yes', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2023-02-22 11:53:24', '2023-02-22 11:53:24', NULL, '104', 'No'),
(18898, 'C2302081004440017', 10, 444, '24', NULL, 'Investigation reveals that the said cardholderÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s credit card statement generation date is 25th of every month as per our bank policy. But in December 2022, cardholderÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s credit card statement was generated on 26th December instead of pre-defined statement date (25th December) due to system glitch. As a result, complaint was raised.', 'The responsible division has already identified the issue and taken appropriate measures to solve it. Hopefully, cardholderÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s credit card statement will be generated on pre-defined date from now onwards. We have already reversed the mentioned cardholderÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s interest which was applied for non-payment of the transaction made on 25th December, 2022. Accordingly, we have replied to Bangladesh bank  through letter ref: MTB/CHO/SQ/2023/10 dated 16 Feb 2023.', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- Yes', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2023-02-22 12:20:33', '2023-02-26 16:41:13', NULL, '104', 'No'),
(18899, 'C2302086002070016', 9, 207, '288', NULL, 'Our investigation reveals that the SMS alert fee was deducted from customerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s account on 30-12-2022. As a result, complaint was raised.', 'The SMS alert fee was deducted from customerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s account on 30-12-2022. However, as per customer request, we have deactivated the SMS alert service and the amount that was deducted in this regard has also been refunded to customerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s account on 22-01-2023. Accordingly, we have replied to BB through letter ref: MTB/CHO/SQ/2023/14 dated 16 Feb 2023', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Mobile Banking', NULL, NULL, '2023-02-22 12:26:14', '2023-02-22 12:26:14', NULL, '28', 'No'),
(18900, 'C2302081005000019', 18, 500, '19', NULL, 'Our investigation reveals that the mentioned cardholder made two transactions (amount of $5.43 and $5.43) at Google on 05-01-2023. But both transaction authorizations have been voided by the merchant (Google). Therefore, the transactions were not settled in customerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s credit card account and did not reflect in his card statement either.', 'The mentioned cardholder made two transactions (amount of $5.43 and $5.43) at Google on 05-01-2023. But both transaction authorizations have been voided by the merchant (Google). Therefore, the transactions were not settled in customerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s credit card account and did not reflect in his card statement either. As such, we are unable to process the chargeback in this regard. Accordingly, We have replied to BB through letter ref: MTB/CHO/SQ/2023/13 dated 16 Feb 2023.', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2023-02-22 12:32:14', '2023-02-22 12:32:14', NULL, '104', 'No'),
(18901, 'N2302080009', 18, 498, '308', NULL, 'Our investigation reveals that the beneficiary is receiving remittance from various sources. The sending address is mentioned as ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã…â€œBangladeshÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã‚Â in last few transactions but the sender is not always the same person. As such, confusion arises whether it is Wage Earners or Freelancer Payment. \r\n\r\nPlease note that, the beneficiary will not receive any cash incentive if it is a Freelancer Payment; but if it is proved that remittance is under Wage Earners, he will get 2.5% cash incentive. Therefore, we have requested the sender to provide further documents (valid work permit or visa). After receiving the required documents from the beneficiary, the concerned department did necessary scrutiny and released the cash incentive on 22-01-2023.', 'The beneficiary is receiving remittance from various sources. The sending address is mentioned as ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã…â€œBangladeshÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã‚Â in last few transactions but the sender is not always the same person. As such, confusion arises whether it is Wage Earners or Freelancer Payment.   Please note that, the beneficiary will not receive any cash incentive if it is a Freelancer Payment; but if it is proved that remittance is under Wage Earners, he will get 2.5% cash incentive. Therefore, we have requested the sender to provide further documents (valid work permit or visa). After receiving the required documents from the beneficiary, the concerned department did necessary scrutiny and released the cash incentive on 22-01-2023. The beneficiary was also informed regarding the incentive release via email. Accordingly, We have replied to BB through letter ref: MTB/CHO/SQ/2023/12 dated 16 Feb 2023.', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Remittance', NULL, NULL, '2023-02-22 12:38:39', '2023-02-22 12:38:39', NULL, '6', 'No'),
