(19051, 'C2302081004440029', 10, 444, '24', NULL, 'The said cardholderÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s credit card statement generation date is 25th of every month as per our bank policy. But in December 2022, cardholderÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s credit card statement was generated on 26th December instead of pre-defined statement date (25th December) due to system glitch.', 'The responsible division has already identified the issue and taken appropriate measures to solve it. Hopefully, cardholderÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s credit card statement will be generated on pre-defined date from now onwards. We have already reversed the mentioned cardholderÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s interest which was applied for non-payment of the transaction made on 25th December, 2022. Accordingly, We have replied to BB through letter ref: MTB/CHO/SQ/2023/11 dated 16 February 2023.', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- Yes', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2023-02-26 16:38:22', '2023-02-26 16:38:22', NULL, '104', 'No'),
(19052, 'N2302140012', 17, 528, '23', NULL, 'Our investigation reveals that our sales agent could not submit the mentioned files to RFC (Retail Financing Center) due to low monthly income of the applicants. But he did not inform it to the applicants within stipulated time. As a result, complaint was raised.', 'Concerned official already apologized to the applicants for the inconvenience and also update the applicants on the current status of their files. It is mentionable here that we have warned the sales agent for his negligence and advised him to be more careful regarding customer communication in the future. Accordingly, We have replied to Bangladesh Bank through letter ref: MTB/CHO/SQ/2023/19 dated 26 Feb 2023.', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- Yes', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2023-02-26 16:46:29', '2023-02-26 16:46:29', NULL, '104', 'No'),
(19053, 'C2302141001990027', 9, 219, '20', NULL, 'According to our annual fee waiver policy, a cardholder will get annual fee waiver if he/ she makes 15 transactions in a year (anniversary to anniversary) and no late payment or over limit fee is imposed in the card account during the same period. \r\n\r\nDue to misunderstanding on customer\'s end, complaint was raised. Our investigation reveals that the said cardholder completed 15 transactions but one late payment was imposed on 10-2-2022.', 'The cardholder requested for reversal of the annual fee, our concerned division considered it and reversed the annual fee as well as the excess limit fee as an exception. Accordingly, We have replied to Bangladesh Bank through letter ref: MTB/CHO/SQ/2023/15 dated 26 Feb 2023', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2023-02-26 16:53:45', '2023-02-26 16:53:45', NULL, '104', 'No'),
(19054, 'C2302142001980028', 7, 337, '228', NULL, 'Customer claimed that he emailed the Tax acknowledgement to our Savar branch but did not get any response. Investigation reveals that we did not find any email from Mr. Asif Parvez via email address: parvez0266@gmail.com.', 'Customer Mr. Asif Parvez visited our Savar branch on 26-01-2023 and submitted his Tax Return acknowledgement copy. Accordingly, we have uploaded it into the system on the same date. Accordingly, We have replied to BB through letter ref: MTB/CHO/SQ/2023/17 dated 26 Feb 23 .', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'General Banking', NULL, NULL, '2023-02-26 16:59:23', '2023-02-26 16:59:23', NULL, '30', 'No'),
(19055, 'C2302142002520029', 10, 443, '169', NULL, 'Investigation reveals that the customer Mr. Md. Saif Uddin Shaju had been maintaining 02 (two) brick by brick (DPS) accounts with our bank since January 2018. Both accounts have matured on December 2022 but were not encashed automatically to his link account due to system glitch.', 'Based on customer request, we have already encashed the mentioned accounts and transferred the amount to customerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s link account on 01-02-2023. Accordingly, we have communicated with customer, informed him about the transfer and also apologized to him for the inconvenience that he had to face. Accordingly, We have replied to BB through letter ref: MTB/CHO/SQ/2023/20 dated 26 Feb 2023.', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'General Banking', NULL, NULL, '2023-02-26 17:08:52', '2023-02-26 17:08:52', NULL, '51', 'No'),
(19056, 'C2302141002190030', 9, 219, '20', NULL, 'According to our annual fee waiver policy, a cardholder will get annual fee waiver if he/ she makes 15 transactions in a year (anniversary to anniversary) and no late payment or over limit fee is imposed in the card account during the same period. This policy is clearly mentioned in our schedule of charges as well as in the credit card application form. \r\n\r\nWe have checked the said cardholderÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s transactions and found that he completed the required number of transactions but three (03) late payment fees were charged against the said credit card. As such, annual fee was imposed.', 'Our concerned division will waive the annual fee as an exception, since the cardholder was unaware of the terms and conditions.  Accordingly, We have replied to BB through letter ref: MTB/CHO/SQ/2023/18 dated 26 Feb 2023 .', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2023-02-26 17:16:25', '2023-02-26 17:16:25', NULL, '104', 'No'),
(19057, 'C2302141002040033', 9, 219, '20', NULL, 'Our investigation reveals that the said cardholderÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s outstanding amount was BDT 336.64 but he deposited BDT 315.00 on 22-12-2022. On 26-12-2022, cardholderÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s credit card statement generated with due amount of BDT 21.73 but Cardholder did not deposit the amount within the due date. That is why late payment fee was imposed on 10-01-2023.', 'The late payment fee was reversed on 06-02-2023 upon cardholderÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s request as an exception. Accordingly, We have replied to BB through letter ref: MTB/CHO/SQ/2023/16 dated 26 Feb 2023', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2023-02-26 17:20:06', '2023-02-26 17:20:06', NULL, '104', 'No'),
(19058, 'C2302141001990034', 9, 204, '20', NULL, 'Our investigation reveals that our bank imposes VAT on transactions associated with Google as per BRPD Circular Letter No 4 dated 03 March 2019. We understand the customerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s concern regarding paying the VAT twice. As Bangladesh Bank has not provided us any instructions regarding VAT reversal, we are now going to send a letter to FEOD (Foreign Exchange Operation Department) of Bangladesh Bank with the documents provided by the cardholder for more clarification regarding VAT reversal issue. After receiving feedback from Bangladesh bank, we will take the decision.', 'Our bank imposes VAT on transactions associated with Google as per BRPD Circular Letter No 4 dated 03 March 2019. We understand the customerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s concern regarding paying the VAT twice. As Bangladesh Bank has not provided us any instructions regarding VAT reversal, we are now going to send a letter to FEOD (Foreign Exchange Operation Department) of Bangladesh Bank with the documents provided by the cardholder for more clarification regarding VAT reversal issue. After receiving feedback from Bangladesh bank, we will take the decision. Accordingly, We have replied to BB through letter ref: MTB/CHO/SQ/2023/21 dated 26 feb 2023.', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2023-02-26 17:23:31', '2023-02-26 17:23:31', NULL, '104', 'No'),
(19059, 'C2302141000930037', 6, 93, '298', NULL, 'Investigation summery is given below: 1.	The Master credit card was blocked by MTB Fraud Risk Management Unit (FRMU) analyst as transaction alert was found through Fraud Detection System (FDS) on 24-01-2023.\r\n2.	Disputed transactions were of e-commerce pattern which took place at NAGAD SSL BD wallet on 24-01-2023 with an amount of BDT 1,50,000/- (BDT 50,000 each) within a short span of time.\r\n3.	Transaction time: 16:39:13, 16:39:28 and 16:39:40 on 24-01-2023.\r\n4.	These were 3D secured/ OTP verified transactions. Record shows that the pertinent OTP was delivered into customerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s registered mobile number (+88 01913030720) prior to executing these transactions.\r\n5.	For all these transactions, the type of service was ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã…â€œAdd money from card to NagadÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã‚Â.\r\n6.	Fraudster made a call to the customer through 16219 (as per CardholderÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s statement) and he (Cardholder) shared all his card credential including OTP with the fraudster. \r\n7.	FRMU also informed the Cardholder that MTB does not make any outgoing call through 16219.', 'MTB FRMU has communicated and shared their findings with the said cardholder regarding these three (03) disputed transactions at Nagad. MTB is not supposed to call the customer from their Contact Centre number (16219) regarding any issue.  Since the cardholder shared his all card credentials including OTP with the fraudster, MTB is not in a position to take any liability & not supposed to refund the customer. However, because of MTBÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s prompt communication with Nagad and the acquiring bank, they were able to hold BDT 1,25,000/- and as per SSL email communication, within the next few days, the customer will get a call from Nagad regarding signing the settlement & declaration letter. Once they receive the signed letter from customer, they will move forward to their next procedure.  However, unless and until this fund is credited to cardholderÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s account, we (MTB) are not in a position to provide the refund confirmation. From MTB, the concerned unit (FRMU) is monitoring the issue with Nagad, SSL & Southeast bank on regular basis until the refund process is completed. Accordingly, We have replied to BB through letter ref: MTB/CHO/SQ/2023/22 dated 26 Feb 2023', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2023-02-26 17:28:05', '2023-02-26 17:28:05', NULL, '104', 'No'),
