(19865, 'C2303141000930045', 6, 93, '298', NULL, 'As per card fraud unit feedback: Dear Concern, please check the attach file about the beneficiary details related documents received from the acquiring bank. After receiving the document from acquiring bank, we have talked with the client about the Nagad account benefiary number (01873667523). As client shared his card credential with the fraudster along with cards OTP, for these circumstances mentioned transactions were took place. We informed client that bank will not take any responsibility regarding this issue as customer card credential information was shared with the fraudster. Cardholder understand that Mutual trust bank will not take any liabilities for such kind of OTP based 3D secured transactions. The cardholder is solely responsible for this incident and the bank will not be responsible under any circumstances. We also mail to the Nagad about that ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã…â€œKindly hold the funds and take necessary steps to reverse the amount to cardholder account. Also requesting to freeze the beneficiary Nagad account where amount was transferred.ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã‚Â Still that we did not receive any feedback from the Nagad about the fund hold issue. If we get any feedback regarding this issue, we will update the client accordingly. We have advised the cardholder when needed, please replace the card through our branch or call center. If customer wants the benefiary details document, please share with her with the respective chaneel.Therefore, based on the above fact findings this review is being closed from FRMU end.', 'Contact Center has already informed this issue to customer regarding the resolution through mail', 0, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Yes', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2023-03-21 15:20:36', '2023-03-21 15:20:36', NULL, '104', 'No'),
