(21037, 'N2304110004', 14, 608, '288', NULL, 'This is to inform you that the customer entered branch premises nearly at the closing time. At that time there was a long queue before cash counter and when his serial came, he placed his money at the cash counter scattered even without mentioning note denominations. The cash officer requested him to tidy up the notes and write down the denominations properly. But the client reacted angrily and did not mean to co-operate the cash officer. Rather he demanded that cash officer should tidy up the notes and write denominations. In response, cash officer further requested him to put his money aside and let the officer allow some time to manage the notes and deposit slip. But the customer did not intend to step aside rather he made barrier for other customer at the queue to do their transactions. At one point, when the customer complained to our Regional Head sir against the respective cash officer, he came to the cash counter hurriedly and personally tried to manage the scattered notes of the customer. Already there became a crowd as other customer had rushed at the branch because business closing time was nearly at end. The customer then yelled at our Regional Head sir for not taking any action against the cash officer and told that he would go further to lodge complain to BB against MTB Sylhet Branch. Regional Head sir then replied that firstly the customer did not follow any rules while depositing money and created chaos at the cash counter and blaming officers instead were really unacceptable from any customer. Moreover, Regional Head sir tried to conciliate the customer and asked him to tidy up the notes but the customer refused to deposit his money and left branch premises.', 'As discussed, we have closed the ticket', 0, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'General Banking', NULL, NULL, '2023-04-18 14:49:25', '2023-04-18 14:49:25', NULL, '28', 'No'),
