(24314, 'C2307082000940009', 6, 94, '298', NULL, 'mentioned transaction was 3D secured E-commerce transaction. Record shows that the pertinent OTP was delivered into customerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s registered mobile number (8801846285706) prior executing this transaction. Customer informed us that fraudster was calling (01923563872) this number related to Banga bazar fire issue as customer is a shopkeeper of Bang bazar market and as client shared his full card number, expiry date, CVV.After that client shared his OTP with the fraudster. For these circumstances mentioned transactions was taken place. Please be informed that mentioned transaction was 3D secured /OTP based transaction, so that, bank will not take any liability as 3D secured /OTP based transaction. We have communicated and share our findings with cardholder regarding disputed transactions at Bkash. Cardholders understand that Mutual trust bank will not take any liabilities for such kind of OTP based 3D secured transaction. The cardholder is solely responsible for this incident and the bank will not be responsible under any circumstances. We have advised the cardholder when needed, please replace the card through our branch or call center. Please be informed that as per statement of Bkash team informed us that any kind of fraud reporting in Bkash they need formal denial letter from customer whether it is handwritten/ Customer registered email for their compliance purpose. Please give us proper written formal letter/ e-mail from Customer registered address where customer will be mentioned that he was not made the mentioned transaction and also mentioned the merchant\'s name & affected the transaction amount with approval code.', 'Contact Center has already informed this issue to customer regarding the resolution', 0, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Yes', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2023-07-12 12:14:07', '2023-07-12 12:14:07', NULL, '104', 'No'),
