(25309, 'C2307136005030031', 18, 503, '42', NULL, 'we have checked the issue and found out that the mentioned NPSB transaction of BDT 300,000/- done on 30-04-2023 and it was successfully credited to beneficiary account. In this regard, our concerned division communicated with customer and updated him.', 'we have checked the issue and found out that the mentioned NPSB transaction of BDT 300,000/- done on 30-04-2023 and it was successfully credited to beneficiary account. In this regard, our concerned division communicated with customer and updated him. Accordingly,We have replied to Bangladesh bank through email dated 01.08.23.', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Internet Banking', NULL, NULL, '2023-08-02 13:46:53', '2023-08-02 13:46:53', NULL, '6', 'No'),
(25310, 'C2307132000210027', 1, 21, '169', NULL, 'we have checked the issue and found that customer Mr. Md Mahmudul Hasan has been maintaining MTB Simple account with our bank. As per regulatory guidelines, the prevailing limit of MTB Simple Account is BDT 1 Lac for both debit and credit transactions, which is mentioned on MTB website. However, it has been observed that customer\'s account has exceeded the total withdrawal limit of BDT 1 Lac in the month of April, 2023 which violated the transaction profile. Therefore, his account transactions have been put on hold. As the account was opened through online platform, the customer needs to visit the branch to regularize the account or convert it into MTB Savings Account to use it as regular one.', 'We have checked the issue and found that customer Mr. Md Mahmudul Hasan has been maintaining MTB Simple account with our bank. As per regulatory guidelines, the prevailing limit of MTB Simple Account is BDT 1 Lac for both debit and credit transactions, which is mentioned on MTB website. However, it has been observed that customer\'s account has exceeded the total withdrawal limit of BDT 1 Lac in the month of April, 2023 which violated the transaction profile. Therefore, his account transactions have been put on hold. As the account was opened through online platform, the customer needs to visit the branch to regularize the account or convert it into MTB Savings Account to use it as regular one. We have communicated with customer in this regard and updated him. We have replied to Bangladesh bank through email dated 01.08.23.', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'General Banking', NULL, NULL, '2023-08-02 13:53:03', '2023-08-02 13:54:48', NULL, '51', 'No'),
(25311, 'C2308012004030030', 8, 403, '174', NULL, 'Branch reply: This account M-easy account . According to rules after account opening customer will be present at Home Branch with his picture and Nominee picture and Sign Also.Customer physically presented 31/07/2023 and as usual we have already send the thanks letter. We verified his address through Thanks letter and then we could withdraw his debit freeze . We cleared concept to customer in this week he will get a thanks letter and acknowledgement recepit back to our end immediately. Now we contact the customer he said he called simply who the opened his account. M-easy account opening officer suggest him the mail contact center. This is absolutely misunderstand customer said now.', 'Branch contacted the customer.', 0, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Yes', NULL, NULL, 'General Banking', NULL, NULL, '2023-08-02 14:01:47', '2023-08-02 14:01:47', NULL, '140', 'No'),
(25312, 'N2307160006', 1, 19, '163', NULL, 'Customer claimed that he is not the director of the company and did not sign at guarantee form. As per our findings, M/s. Hi-Ton Industrial Corporation Ltd. was sanctioned composite credit limit of Tk 85 M (funded Tk 75 M) on 04.05.2015 and the facility was renewed every year till 2019. At that time, the company had five directors. As per our record we found the following information in response to the letter of Mr. Md. Jasim Uddin: \r\n\r\n(a)	In the Board resolution of the company for obtaining loan, Mr. Md. Jasim Uddin has signed as one of the directors of the company. \r\n\r\n(b)	Mr. Jasim Uddin has signed in DP note and Personal Guarantee which was verified by concerned credit officer of the branch. \r\n\r\n(c)	In the letter dated 14.06.2023, Mr. Jasim mentioned that he came to know about the loan after serving legal notice to Mr. Md. Abul Kalam (one of the directors) as on 22.05.2023. But we also served legal notice to all directors in 2021 before filing suit under NI Act. \r\n\r\n(d)	Mr. Jasim came to the branch & meet Branch Manager on 24.07.2023 and on conversation he informed that earlier he came to the branch (in 2021 during the tenor of previous BM) and took information about loan. \r\n\r\n(e)	Mr. Jasim did not take NOC from MTB prior transferring his share and neither submitted any up to date documents from RJSC regarding his resignation from the company.', 'We have replied to Bangladesh bank as per response received from concerned branch.', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Loans and Advances', NULL, NULL, '2023-08-02 14:04:17', '2023-08-02 14:04:17', NULL, '21', 'No'),
(25313, 'C2307281006290023', 13, 629, '18', NULL, 'His Arrival Date of Service 2023-07-28 and Arrival Pickup Time 06:30 PM. He call driver for this service and Driver confirmed he arrived for this service at 06:30AM. for this miscommunication raised.', 'Card business team make the customer understand.', 0, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Yes', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2023-08-02 14:55:42', '2023-08-02 14:55:42', NULL, '104', 'No'),
