(25571, 'C2308021004040030', 8, 404, '23', NULL, 'Card sales didn\'t marked as GP star by mistake.', 'VISA SIG CRED GENERAL to VISA SIGNATURE CREDIT GP as per approval and mark 1st year free. CC informed the customer.', 0, 'Yes', NULL, NULL, 'Yes', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2023-08-09 10:44:39', '2023-08-09 10:44:39', NULL, '104', 'No'),
(25572, 'N2307260005', 1, 19, '62', NULL, 'As an IT service provider,  M/S TechNickel  is enjoying cash incentive facility @ 10% as per instructions of attached F E Circular # 03, Dated, February 08, 2018. In availing cash incentive facility, it is the prerequisite that, service export has to submit cash incentive application within 180 days from the date of remittance received. Investigation reveals that M/S TechNickel failed to submit applications against 14 invoices, having export value USD 131,895.86 within the legitimate timeframe as prescribed in the FE Circular. Due to failure to submit applications within 180 days from the date of remittance received, these applications are not eligible for cash incentive certifications.', 'M/s TechNicle send a letter to Office of the honorable Governor of Bangladesh Bank, Director- FICSD & Director ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Å“ FEPD of Bangladesh Bank explaining the reasons behind non-submission of applications in due time and approval for allowing those applications for certification. We are awaiting for the valuable decision/direction of the honorable GovernorÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s office, Director- FICSD & Director ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Å“ FEPD in this regard.  They have mentioned in their letter that, a letter sent to Bangladesh Bank through Office of Managing Director & CEO of Mutual Trust Bank Limited. But we couldn\'t send letter via us due shortage of complete applications which we suggested them to submit through telephonic conversation. Accordingly, We have replied to Bangladesh bank through email dated 08 Aug 2023.', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Remittance', NULL, NULL, '2023-08-09 10:44:39', '2023-08-09 10:44:39', NULL, '113', 'No'),
(25573, 'C2307262003650035', 7, 365, '285', NULL, 'SMS and email enrollment is okay.', 'CC tried to reach the customer but failed.', 0, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Yes', NULL, NULL, 'General Banking', NULL, NULL, '2023-08-09 10:52:19', '2023-08-09 10:52:19', NULL, '133', 'No'),
(25574, 'C2307262002270026', 9, 218, '164', NULL, 'we have checked the issue and found out that the customer has been maintaining a savings account in MTB Dhanmondi Branch and on 10-07-2023 she placed a request to de-enroll SMS banking service for the said account through our Contact Centre. Accordingly, the concerned branch de-enrolled the SMS service as per customer request. In addition, our concerned branch also reversed SMS banking charges of BDT 930.43/- on 27-07-23.', 'we have checked the issue and found out that the customer has been maintaining a savings account in MTB Dhanmondi Branch and on 10-07-2023 she placed a request to de-enroll SMS banking service for the said account through our Contact Centre. Accordingly, the concerned branch de-enrolled the SMS service as per customer request. In addition, our concerned branch also reversed SMS banking charges of BDT 930.43/- on 27-07-23. We have communicated with customer and updated her. We have also replied to Bangladesh bank through email dated 08 Aug 2023.', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'General Banking', NULL, NULL, '2023-08-09 10:54:30', '2023-08-09 10:54:30', NULL, '19', 'No'),
(25575, 'C2307272004830036', 12, 483, '297', NULL, 'When the first transaction was initiated on August 20, 2022, the beneficiary account information was incorrectly provided(digit mismatch) by CRFCD to JP Morgan Chase Bank. After that, on September 5, 2022, the re-remittance messages (MTB a/c details) were given (twice) wrongly by CRFCD, for which they sent a \"NULL & VOID\" request against one transaction to the correspondent bank, but it was not executed, moreover, CRFCD did not follow up on whether the request was honored. While the centralized remittance team was informed by the Financial Market Operations Department (FMOD) on July 5, 2023 after 10 months, Ms. Jannatunnesa of your team communicated with the customer over phone (instead of taking any formal request) and informed him to settle the duplicate transaction of GBP 3700.00 either locally or recalling it through JP Morgan, but again, she made another mistake by providing wrong information to the customer about the fund (with wrong conversion rate). She has made mistakes repeatedly which caused the customer furious and highly dissatisfied with our services!', 'Concerned department apologized to the customer. Email is attached herewith.', 0, 'Yes', NULL, NULL, 'Yes', NULL, NULL, 'General Banking', NULL, NULL, '2023-08-09 11:04:10', '2023-08-13 12:33:00', NULL, '6', 'No'),
(25576, 'C2308076000630008', 4, 63, '42', NULL, 'dig banking reply: There was a technical issue with the OTP which is solved now. Please ask customer to try again', 'OB tried to reach customer several times but was unreachable', 0, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Yes', NULL, NULL, 'Internet Banking', NULL, NULL, '2023-08-09 11:09:51', '2023-08-09 11:09:51', NULL, '6', 'Yes'),
