(26835, 'C2308271004840033', 12, 484, '20', NULL, 'We have checked the issue and found that customer made a bill payment query (BDT & USD part) through other bank EFT to our contact centre on 31-07-23. Our contact centre executive informed customer about the details and also requested to make a call for credit balance transfer (BDT to USD) after updating the payment. As per our process, if customer wants to pay the USD part bill through EFT from other bank, at first the amount will be credited to cardÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s BDT part and after that credit balance transfer (BDT to USD) will be done according to customerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s instruction.\r\nNonetheless, customer paid the bill on 01-08-23 and the amount was credited on the same date at the BDT part of his credit card. But customer requested for credit balance transfer (BDT to USD) on 10-08-23. Please note that the USD conversion rate as on 01-08-23 was lower than the conversion rate of 10-08-23. As customer requested to transfer the USD part bill on 10-08-23, the exchange rate of the transaction date (10-08-23) was applied. Therefore, confusion arose due to the fluctuation of exchange rate.', 'Customer paid the bill on 01-08-23 and the amount was credited on the same date at the BDT part of his credit card. But customer requested for credit balance transfer (BDT to USD) on 10-08-23. Please note that the USD conversion rate as on 01-08-23 was lower than the conversion rate of 10-08-23. As customer requested to transfer the USD part bill on 10-08-23, the exchange rate of the transaction date (10-08-23) was applied. Therefore, confusion arose due to the fluctuation of exchange rate. However, we have again communicated with customer and explained him in detail about the process and exchange rate. Customer is convinced now and the issue is resolved. Accordingly, we have replied to Bangladesh Bank through email dated 12 September 2023.', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2023-09-12 13:23:00', '2023-09-12 13:23:00', NULL, '104', 'No'),
