(28489, 'N2310160015', 1, 19, '48', NULL, 'Our concerned division, Group Finance (Capital Management & Investment) have checked the issue and informed us that they are already aware of the situation. Here, It\'s important to note that MTB, like other investors, is facing challenges in this matter. MTB is an investor in the open-end mutual/unit fund, where it holds a 20% stake as a sponsor investor. However, under the prevailing rules of BSEC, after launching the fund the responsibility for investment management and investor relations lies with other parties, including the Asset Manager (Alliance Capital Asset Management Ltd), Trustee, and Custodian of the fund. \r\n\r\nRecently, there was an financial embezzlement within this unit fund, and the asset manager, Alliance Capital Asset Management Ltd, was found responsible for this delinquency. This came to light during a regulatory investigation by the Bangladesh Securities and Exchange Commission (BSEC), leading to the freezing of all accounts and funds belonging to Alliance Capital Asset Management Ltd. Consequently, all investors are currently unable to redeem their investments from this fund.\r\n\r\nMTB requested the asset manager several times through letter, email and verbal communication to return the invested fund, but in response, they stated that they are currently unable to redeem the fund due to the restrictions imposed by BSEC.\r\n\r\nIn light of these circumstances, it is to inform that MTB is not responsible for entertaining any investor and  reimbursing their  funds. Individual investors should contact Alliance Capital Asset Management Limited or the fund\'s Trustee to facilitate the return of their invested funds.', 'It is to inform that MTB is not responsible for entertaining any investor and  reimbursing their  funds. Individual investors should contact Alliance Capital Asset Management Limited or the fund\'s Trustee to facilitate the return of their invested funds.', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Miscellaneous', NULL, NULL, '2023-10-22 16:12:08', '2023-10-22 16:12:08', NULL, '6', 'No'),
