(30444, 'N2311140006', 1, 19, '63', NULL, 'Our client Oxford Shirt Ltd. and Oxford Knit Composite Ltd. received two export order through the said buying House D- Fashion Ltd. During the execution of 1st contract the said buying house placed another contract and our client asked for the pending export from old contract first. In response to that persuasion D-Fashion undertake to arrange the pending shipment and requested the client/exporter to take new order. The buyer took the export of 2nd order partially but made the payment after long time and they are yet to take the shipment form the 1st contract of $ 5,91,818.75. Our client is negatively impacted due to the failure of D Fashion /their buyer to keep their commitment regarding the shipment and payment. After receiving the complaint, we have again sent the email to concerned division. After communicating with the client, related lawyer and as per previous communication, their response are given below: ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã‚Â¢ Legal Notice: As an initial step of legal action, nominated lawyer of Oxford Shirt Ltd. has issued the legal notice to hold the buying house commission against the export of Oxford Knit Composite Ltd. allied concern of the same group. This two concerns are availing credit facility from MTB under single credit approval/sanction. After receiving the legal notice we have already talked to the concerned lawyer Mr. Zahirul Islam and he said that receiver no. 5.00 [ M/s D Fashions] is the mail counterparty related to the loss incurred by MTB Client Oxford Shirt Ltd. and the other receivers [Bangladesh Bank and Mutual Trust Bank Ltd. (Currently Mutual Trust Bank PLC)] are only the notifying party here so that we can take necessary measure about the issue. ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã‚Â¢ Current Status of the issue: Along with legal action client is also raised the issue to BGMEA for arbitration and BGMEA has already issued 2 letters to the related parties. [Related communication attached[. ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã‚Â¢ Concluding Remarks: As the buying house is not taking the export from Oxford Shirt Ltd. [OSL] even after undertaking and completing the inspection, the borrower [OSL] is incurring the loss and facing difficulty to repay the bank liability as they have already procured raw material through BTB LC. Therefore MTB has kept the said buying house commission in blocked account but it will be released after the pending shipment/ legal consequence/BGMEA arbitration decision issues are resolved.', 'As the buying house is not taking the export from Oxford Shirt Ltd. [OSL] even after undertaking and completing the inspection, the borrower [OSL] is incurring the loss and facing difficulty to repay the bank liability as they have already procured raw material through BTB LC. Therefore MTB has kept the said buying house commission in blocked account but it will be released after the pending shipment/ legal consequence/BGMEA arbitration decision issues are resolved.', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Export Related', NULL, NULL, '2023-12-03 16:32:36', '2023-12-03 16:32:36', NULL, '6', 'No'),
(30445, 'C2311291000440039', 3, 44, '36', NULL, 'CC reply: Previously customer made several successful POS transaction in different POS. It might be acquirer or POS issue. If the card is physically ok it should work, or ch may replace the card with charge.', 'OB informed customer accordingly', 0, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Yes', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2023-12-03 16:37:46', '2023-12-03 16:37:46', NULL, '116', 'No'),
