(31579, 'C2312211002040031', 9, 219, '20', NULL, 'Cardholder requested for annual fee waiver. We have checked the matter and found that cardholder completed the required number of transactions, but five (05) late payment fees were imposed against the credit card. As such, he is not eligible for reversal as per our annual fee waiver policy.', 'Cardholder completed the required number of transactions, but five (05) late payment fees were imposed against the credit card. As such, he is not eligible for reversal as per our annual fee waiver policy. Accordingly, we replied back to Bangladesh bank through email dated 03-01-2023.', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2024-01-03 17:10:57', '2024-01-03 17:10:57', NULL, '104', 'No'),
(31580, 'C2312211002040033', 9, 219, '20', NULL, 'Due to impose of MPP fee, complaint was raised. MTB Protection Plan is an insurance coverage program offered to all credit cardholders. A cardholder will be automatically enrolled to MPP after he or she has been issued card and it is duly mentioned in our website. However, if any cardholder is not willing to avail the insurance coverage then he/she may de-enroll the plan. In this connection, the MTB Protection Plan (MPP) fee of BDT 534.19 has already been reversed to customerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s card account on 06-12-2023 and our concerned division also de-enrolled the MTB Protection Plan (MPP) as per customer request.', 'The MTB Protection Plan (MPP) fee of BDT 534.19 has already been reversed to customerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s card account on 06-12-2023 and our concerned division also de-enrolled the MTB Protection Plan (MPP) as per customer request. Accordingly, we replied to Bangladesh Bank through email dated 03-01-2024.', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2024-01-03 17:32:41', '2024-01-03 17:32:41', NULL, '104', 'No'),
(31581, 'C2312211002040032', 9, 219, '20', NULL, 'Due to imposed of Annual fee, complaint was raised. The annual fee of BDT 11,500/- was charged against customerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s credit card on 23-11-2023. Cardholder completed required number of transactions but one late payment fee charged on October 2023. However, annual fee has been reversed to customerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s card account on 13-12-2023 as an exception.', 'Cardholder completed required number of transactions but one late payment fee charged on October 2023. However, annual fee has been reversed to customerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s card account on 13-12-2023 as an exception. Accordingly, we replied to Bangladesh Bank through email dated 03-01-2024.', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2024-01-03 17:41:19', '2024-01-03 17:41:19', NULL, '104', 'No'),
(31582, 'C2312211002040035', 9, 219, '20', NULL, 'Due to impose of Annual fee, complaint was raised. We have checked the issue and found that cardholderÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s first year annual fee was free (credit card issue date-16-11-2022) and second year annual fee charged on 23-11-2023. Cardholder did not complete required number of transactions within first year that is why he is not eligible for reversal as per our annual fee waiver policy. We have communicated with customer and updated him.\r\n\r\nAccording to our annual fee waiver policy, a cardholder will get annual fee waiver if he/ she makes 15 transactions in a year (anniversary to anniversary) and no late payment or over limit fee is imposed in the card account during the same period. This policy is clearly mentioned in our schedule of charges as well as in the credit card application form.', 'We have checked the issue and found that cardholderÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s first year annual fee was free (credit card issue date-16-11-2022) and second year annual fee charged on 23-11-2023. Cardholder did not complete required number of transactions within first year that is why he is not eligible for reversal as per our annual fee waiver policy. We have communicated with customer and updated him.', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'Debit Card or Credit Card or ATM Card', NULL, NULL, '2024-01-03 17:46:57', '2024-01-03 17:46:57', NULL, '104', 'No'),
(31583, 'C2312212004670036', 10, 467, '175', NULL, 'We have checked the issue and found that the customer Mr. AHM Shahedul Alom maintained an MTB simple account with us from 10-10-2023. The transaction limit of MTB simple account is BDT 1,00,000/-. As per policy, If the limit exceeds, the account will be frozen automatically. CustomerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s MTB simple account transaction limit has exceeded, therefore the account got frozen automatically as per process. However, customer submitted necessary documents and converted his MTB simple account to an MTB regular savings account. Now, customerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s savings account is activated and he is doing regular transactions.', 'Customer submitted necessary documents and converted his MTB simple account to an MTB regular savings account. Now, customerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s savings account is activated and he is doing regular transactions. Accordingly, we replied to Bangladesh bank through email dated 03-01-2024 .', 0, 'Bangladesh Bank- No', NULL, NULL, 'No', NULL, NULL, 'General Banking', NULL, NULL, '2024-01-03 17:51:51', '2024-01-03 17:51:51', NULL, '12', 'No'),
